  <!-- Service Types Detail -->
  <section id="services" class="bg-[#F8F8F5] py-20">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-14">
        <p class="text-[#9A9D62] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm mb-3">Commercial Entry Expertise</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Office Lockout Services We Provide</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          From standard office entry to high-security commercial hardware and electronic access bypass, our commercial locksmiths handle every business lockout situation throughout Delaware.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">

        <!-- Card 1 -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M2.25 21h19.5m-18-18v18m10.5-18v18m6-13.5V21M6.75 6.75h.75m-.75 3h.75m-.75 3h.75m3-6h.75m-.75 3h.75m-.75 3h.75M6.75 21v-3.375c0-.621.504-1.125 1.125-1.125h2.25c.621 0 1.125.504 1.125 1.125V21M3 3h12m-.75 4.5H21m-3.75 3.75h.008v.008h-.008v-.008zm0 3h.008v.008h-.008v-.008zm0 3h.008v.008h-.008v-.008z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Standard Office & Storefront Lockout</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Office doors and storefront entries most commonly use cylindrical locksets or mortise locks â€” commercial-grade hardware that requires more specific tools and technique than standard residential locks. Our technicians carry commercial-specific pick sets and bypass tools for these lock types.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            We open Schlage, Kwikset Commercial, Corbin Russwin, Yale, BEST, and other common commercial lock brands without damage to the door, frame, or hardware. Our goal is to have you operational as quickly as possible with no repair work needed afterward.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            If the lockout involves a lost key or security concern, we recommend a <a href="/services/commercial-lock-rekeying/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">commercial lock rekey</a> on the same visit so you are not left wondering who else may have access.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 2 -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M17.25 6.75L22.5 12l-5.25 5.25m-10.5 0L1.5 12l5.25-5.25m7.5-3l-4.5 16.5" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Electronic Keypad & Access Control Lockout</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Businesses with electronic keypad entry or access control systems face a different kind of lockout â€” forgotten codes, dead batteries, card reader failures, or system malfunctions. These situations require a different approach than mechanical lock picking.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            We assess the specific access control system and determine the fastest and least disruptive path to entry. In many cases, we can bypass or override the electronic system to regain access. If the hardware requires replacement or reprogramming, we document and advise before any work begins.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            For ongoing electronic access control needs â€” installing, upgrading, or adding <a href="/services/deadbolt-installation/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">additional deadbolt hardware</a> as a backup â€” we provide full commercial locksmith consultation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 3 -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15.75 5.25a3 3 0 013 3m3 0a6 6 0 01-7.029 5.912c-.563-.097-1.159.026-1.563.43L10.5 17.25H8.25v2.25H6v2.25H2.25v-2.818c0-.597.237-1.17.659-1.591l6.499-6.499c.404-.404.527-1 .43-1.563A6 6 0 1121.75 8.25z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Post-Termination Security Lockout</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            When an employee is terminated â€” especially one who had key access to your facility â€” the security priority is immediate. If keys were not returned, or if there is any reason to believe they might have been copied, your business is at risk until the locks are changed.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            We respond to these situations quickly, arriving to rekey or replace all affected locks before the business day is done. Rekeying is usually the fastest and most cost-effective solution â€” it invalidates the old key and issues new ones without replacing any hardware.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            For businesses that want a comprehensive security review after a personnel change â€” including assessing whether a <a href="/services/master-key-systems/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">master key system</a> would improve access control â€” we offer on-site security consultations with our commercial service.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 4 -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3.75 21h16.5M4.5 3h15M5.25 3v18m13.5-18v18M9 6.75h1.5m-1.5 3h1.5m-1.5 3h1.5m3-6H15m-1.5 3H15m-1.5 3H15M9 21v-3.375c0-.621.504-1.125 1.125-1.125h3.75c.621 0 1.125.504 1.125 1.125V21" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Interior Office & Server Room Lockout</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Not all office lockouts are at the front door. Businesses frequently find themselves locked out of interior spaces â€” private offices, server rooms, storage closets, executive suites, or file rooms. These interior doors often use smaller cylindrical locksets or privacy knobs that require specific pick tools.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            We handle interior commercial door locks for all common hardware types. In many cases, interior doors can be opened quickly without any damage â€” the same professional pick-and-bypass approach we use at exterior entry doors. We always attempt non-destructive entry first.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            If you find yourself locked out of a filing cabinet or storage vault rather than a door, we also handle commercial storage lockouts and can assess whether the lock needs replacement or can be repaired after entry.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 5 -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M11.42 15.17L17.25 21A2.652 2.652 0 0021 17.25l-5.877-5.877M11.42 15.17l2.496-3.03c.317-.384.74-.626 1.208-.766M11.42 15.17l-4.655 5.653a2.548 2.548 0 11-3.586-3.586l6.837-5.63m5.108-.233c.55-.164 1.163-.188 1.743-.14a4.5 4.5 0 004.486-6.336l-3.276 3.277a3.004 3.004 0 01-2.25-2.25l3.276-3.276a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.336 4.486c.091 1.076-.071 2.264-.904 2.95l-.102.085m-1.745 1.437L5.909 7.5H4.5L2.25 3.75l1.5-1.5L7.5 4.5v1.409l4.26 4.26m-1.745 1.437l1.745-1.437m6.615 8.206L15.75 15.75M4.867 19.125h.008v.008h-.008v-.008z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Broken Key in Commercial Lock</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            A key that breaks off in a commercial door lock is especially disruptive â€” particularly at the front door of a business that needs to open for customers. The broken fragment must be removed before any key, including a spare, will work, and attempting removal with improvised tools is almost always counterproductive.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Our technicians carry dedicated <a href="/services/broken-key-extraction/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">broken key extraction</a> tools for both residential and commercial cylinders. We remove the fragment cleanly, assess the cylinder condition, and get you operational immediately â€” in most cases without any need for lock replacement.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            If the cylinder was damaged during the break or by prior attempts at extraction, we can install a replacement cylinder in the existing lock hardware so you are back in business without a full door hardware replacement.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 6 -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 6v6h4.5m4.5 0a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Early Morning & After-Hours Office Lockout</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Business lockouts do not limit themselves to 9-to-5. A restaurant needs to open at 6 AM. A retail store has staff arriving before the manager. A warehouse runs second and third shifts. We maintain 6 days a week availability precisely because business operations run 6 days a week.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            We dispatch quickly and our pricing is fair and disclosed before we begin work.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            For a comprehensive look at what we offer Delaware businesses beyond emergency entry â€” including <a href="/services/commercial-locksmith/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">commercial locksmith services</a>, access control, and lock upgrades â€” visit our commercial locksmith page.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

